<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Hunyadi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1406–<a href="/years/1456">1456</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Hunyadi János, Iancu de Hunedoara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Hunyadi was a Hungarian general and nobleman of Wallachian origin who led the fight against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. He was voivode of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> from 1441, ban of Severin and regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1446 to 1453. His victory at the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> in 1456 halted the Ottoman advance for decades, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a> became king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-hunyadi.jpg" alt="John Hunyadi" width="320" height="365" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: János Thuróczy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Hunyadi_(Chronica_Hungarorum).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
